# Cursor rules — spectacles-unitree (monorepo)

This repository combines the DimOS AR bridge (`dimos-ar/`) and the Spectacles
Lens client (`lens-studio/`). It is **not a fork of DimOS** — a separate package
that depends on DimOS and composes into blueprints via `autoconnect`.

## Layout

```text
spectacles-unitree/
├── README.md                    # whole-project overview, setup, doc map
├── assets/                      # README gifs, demo media (NOT Lens Studio Assets/)
├── dimos-ar/                    # Python DimOS extension (platform-agnostic core)
│   ├── dimos_ar/                # ARBridge module, protocol, transforms, filters
│   ├── blueprints/              # go2_ar_basic.py (M1), go2_ar_nav.py (M2+, planned)
│   ├── clients/
│   │   ├── web/                 # Vite + Three.js debug / phone client
│   │   └── marker/              # QR marker page served by start.sh
│   ├── scripts/                 # generate_marker.py (--sync-lens)
│   ├── docs/                    # PROJECT_BRIEF, ARCHITECTURE, PROTOCOL, LENS_DEVELOPMENT, MARKER_ASSETS
│   ├── tests/                   # pytest unit + optional WS integration
│   ├── start.sh                 # discover Go2 or replay; WebSocket on :8765
│   └── .cursorrules             # Python / bridge rules
└── lens-studio/                 # Spectacles Lens Studio project
    ├── spectacles-unitree.esproj   # open THIS file (never from repo root)
    ├── Assets/Scripts/          # Lens TypeScript (DimosManager, BridgeClient, …)
    ├── docs/SCENE_SETUP.md      # scene wiring checklist
    ├── tools/                   # dev helpers (e.g. create_debug_gizmo.py)
    └── .cursorrules             # Lens Studio rules
```

| Component | Location | Notes |
|-----------|----------|-------|
| `ARBridge`, protocol, transforms | `dimos-ar/dimos_ar/` | Platform-agnostic — no Spectacles logic |
| Blueprint scripts | `dimos-ar/blueprints/` | Run on Mac with DimOS |
| Web debug / phone client | `dimos-ar/clients/web/` | Reference protocol implementation |
| Spectacles Lens | `lens-studio/` | All Lens Studio code; see `LENS_DEVELOPMENT.md` |
| Cross-platform contract | `dimos-ar/docs/PROTOCOL.md` | JSON WebSocket API |

## Where to read first

| Area | Read |
|------|------|
| Whole project | `README.md` |
| Goals & milestones | `dimos-ar/docs/PROJECT_BRIEF.md` |
| Package design & threading | `dimos-ar/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| WebSocket message schema | `dimos-ar/docs/PROTOCOL.md` |
| Spectacles / Lens Studio | `dimos-ar/docs/LENS_DEVELOPMENT.md`, `dimos-ar/docs/MARKER_ASSETS.md`, `lens-studio/docs/SCENE_SETUP.md` |
| Contributing | `CONTRIBUTING.md` |
| Python / bridge work | `dimos-ar/.cursorrules` |
| Lens Studio work | `lens-studio/.cursorrules` |

## Non-negotiable facts

- **Never edit DimOS source.** Import from the installed `dimos` package.
- `dimos-ar/dimos_ar/` stays platform-agnostic. Spectacles-specific code lives
  only under `lens-studio/`.
- **Open Lens Studio from `lens-studio/spectacles-unitree.esproj`**, not the repo
  root — opening at root creates stray `Cache/`, `Packages/`, etc.
- The cross-repo contract is `dimos-ar/docs/PROTOCOL.md`. When the protocol
  changes, update all four in the same change:
  - `dimos-ar/dimos_ar/protocol.py`
  - `dimos-ar/docs/PROTOCOL.md`
  - `dimos-ar/clients/web/src/protocol.ts`
  - `lens-studio/Assets/Scripts/Network/Protocol.ts`
- The bridge module worker must never block; WebSocket runs on a daemon thread
  (see `dimos-ar/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`).
- AR development uses `dimos-ar/blueprints/go2_ar_basic.py` (via `./start.sh`),
  not the stock `dimos --replay run unitree-go2` CLI alone.
- Port **8765** is ARBridge WebSocket. Do not run DimOS Foxglove on the same port.

## Dev quick reference

```bash
# Install + start bridge (from dimos-ar/)
./start.sh              # LAN discovery or replay; ws://0.0.0.0:8765
./start.sh --replay       # replay only
./start.sh --local        # localhost-only WebSocket

# Web debug client
cd dimos-ar/clients/web && npm install && npm run dev

# Tests (with blueprint running for integration)
cd dimos-ar && pytest
cd dimos-ar && pytest tests/test_ws_integration.py -m integration
```
